## 16\. Testing Completion Criteria

 Testing can be considered complete when:

 - Critical functional tests pass.
- Gemini integration works reliably under expected conditions.
- Generated content can be edited and regenerated.
- Projects can be saved and retrieved.
- Major UI issues are resolved.
- Error handling works appropriately.
- No unresolved critical defects remain.
- User acceptance testing meets the project's defined requirements.

